The task is the classic nested-parentheses parser. I’m using the canonical contract interpretation: split on literal spaces, scan each group, track current and maximum depth, and emit one integer per split field. That matches Python’s `str.split(" ")` behavior—including empty fields—and avoids baking the expected answer into the implementation.
